## Not in this list (deliberately)
- **Verify intent first, not blind-fix:** Container Apps public-internet exposure (9 — some are meant to be public SaaS endpoints); PostgreSQL Entra-only auth (2 — may break password-auth callers).
- **Exempting, not fixing:** pgaudit recs (PIM activation-logging is our compensating control); Defender paid-plan upsells (cost decision, pending).
- **Lane A overlap (dep-bump flow, not here):** AKS node vuln findings (2), ACR image vulnerabilities (1).

## Notes
- Enabling the **AKS Azure Policy add-on** is the single highest-leverage move — once Gatekeeper enforces the pod-security baseline, the automount / privesc / read-only-FS / limits items (~150 findings combined) clear together rather than one workload at a time.
- Bulk diagnostic-logging (58) is best done with an Azure **Policy DeployIfNotExists** assignment so new resources auto-onboard, not per-resource by hand.
